23. AUTOMATION FRAMEWORK 🔴
422. What is an automation framework?
Interview answer

An automation framework is a structured set of guidelines, reusable components, utilities, coding standards, and tools used to develop and maintain automated test cases efficiently.

In my framework, I separate test cases from page-level actions, driver management, test data, configuration, utilities, reporting, logging, and common reusable methods.

The main goal is reusability, maintainability, scalability, parallel execution, and easy debugging.

Example

Instead of writing this in every test:

driver.findElement(By.id("username")).sendKeys("admin");
driver.findElement(By.id("password")).sendKeys("password");
driver.findElement(By.id("login")).click();

I create:

loginPage.login(username, password);

This makes the test cleaner and easier to maintain.

