Each module has reusable methods.

3. Data-driven framework

Test data is separated from test logic.

Example:

username | password
user1    | pass1
user2    | pass2
user3    | pass3
4. Keyword-driven framework

Actions are represented using keywords:

CLICK
TYPE
SELECT
VERIFY
5. Hybrid framework

Combines multiple approaches.

For example:

POM
+
Data Driven
+
TestNG
+
Utilities
+
Reporting
+
CI/CD
6. BDD framework

Uses tools such as Cucumber.

Given user is on login page
When user enters valid credentials
Then user should see dashboard
Strong interview answer

In real projects, I prefer a hybrid framework, usually combining Page Object Model, data-driven testing, reusable utilities, TestNG, reporting, logging, configuration management, and CI/CD integration.

