441. What is Retry mechanism?

Retry mechanism reruns failed tests automatically when appropriate.

Example:

public class RetryAnalyzer implements IRetryAnalyzer {

    private int count = 0;
    private int maxRetry = 2;

    @Override
    public boolean retry(ITestResult result) {

        if (count < maxRetry) {
            count++;
            return true;
        }

        return false;
    }
}
Important interview point

Don't say:

"I retry every failed test."

Instead:

I use retry selectively. I first investigate whether the failure is a genuine product defect or a transient automation/environment issue. Retry should not be used to hide real defects.

That's a strong SDET answer.

442. How do you implement parallel execution?

TestNG allows parallel execution.

Example:

<suite name="Regression" parallel="tests" thread-count="4">

Possible levels:

methods
tests
classes

Example:

parallel="tests"
thread-count="4"

means up to four tests can execute concurrently.

Benefits
500 tests sequentially
        ↓
Very long execution

Parallel execution
        ↓
Reduced execution time

But parallel execution requires:

thread-safe driver
isolated test data
no shared mutable state
thread-safe utilities
443. What is ThreadLocal WebDriver?

This is very important for SDET interviews.

When tests run in parallel, we should not allow multiple threads to share the same WebDriver.

Instead:

Thread 1 → Chrome 1
Thread 2 → Chrome 2
Thread 3 → Chrome 3
Thread 4 → Chrome 4

Using:

private static ThreadLocal<WebDriver> driver =
        new ThreadLocal<>();

Example:

public class DriverManager {

    private static ThreadLocal<WebDriver> driver =
            new ThreadLocal<>();

    public static void setDriver(WebDriver webDriver) {
        driver.set(webDriver);
    }

    public static WebDriver getDriver() {
        return driver.get();
    }

    public static void unload() {
        driver.remove();
    }
}
Why?

Without ThreadLocal:

Thread 1 ─┐
Thread 2 ─┼──> Same driver ❌
Thread 3 ─┘

Potential problems:

wrong browser
wrong page
session conflicts
test interference

With ThreadLocal:

Thread 1 → Driver 1
Thread 2 → Driver 2
Thread 3 → Driver 3

Much safer for parallel execution.

