🔥 VERY IMPORTANT: "Explain your framework" — 2-minute answer

If the interviewer says:

"Okay, explain your automation framework."

Give this answer:

"I have worked with a hybrid Selenium Java framework using TestNG and Page Object Model.

The framework is divided into different layers. Test classes contain the actual test scenarios, while page classes contain locators and page-specific actions. We have a BasePage for common Selenium operations such as click, type, wait, and element handling.

Driver creation is centralized in DriverFactory, and for parallel execution we use ThreadLocal WebDriver so each thread gets its own browser session.

Configuration such as browser, environment and URLs is externalized rather than hardcoded. Test data is also maintained separately using appropriate data sources such as JSON, Excel, CSV or APIs depending on the requirement.

We use TestNG for test execution, annotations, groups, DataProvider and parallel execution. Listeners are used for failure handling, screenshots and reporting. Logging is implemented to help with debugging.

The framework is integrated with Maven, Git and Jenkins. Jenkins can trigger smoke or regression suites based on parameters, and the execution results are published through reports.

The main objective of the framework is maintainability, reusability, scalability, parallel execution and easy failure analysis."

